        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ann Beattie; Edgar Rice Burroughs\n- Works: Chilly Scenes of Winter; The Oakdale Affair and The Rider\n- Companies: Doubleday\n- Roles: Novelist; short story writer; fiction writer\n- Topics: Adventure fiction; science fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Edgar Rice Burroughs was born on September 1, 1875, and he died on March 19, 1950.\n- Ann Beattie was born on September 8, 1947.\n- Edgar Rice Burroughs was an American fiction writer best known for his prolific work in the adventure and science-fiction genres.\n- Chilly Scenes of Winter is Ann Beattie’s first novel, and Doubleday published it in September 1976.\n- The Oakdale Affair and The Rider is a collection of two short novels by Edgar Rice Burroughs.\n- Ann Beattie is an American novelist and short story writer.",
